        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "FCC1 pin 48 VCAP → UART3_TX_FCC; pin 73 VCAP → UART3_RX_FCC (FCC sheet, page 2/6)."
        },
        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "NAVC1 pin 31 VCAP_1 → I2C3_SDA_NAVC; pin 47 VCAP_2 → UART3_TX_NAVC (NAVC sheet, page 3/6)."
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "FCC1: STM32H753VITx; NAVC1: STM32F405RGTx (Component Table, Hades)."
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The VCAP pins support the MCUs' internal core regulators. Connecting them to external signal nets and omitting their required capacitors can prevent reliable operation or startup of both MCUs, while also loading or corrupting the connected signals.",
      "confidence": 0.99
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Both MCU designs connect internal VCAP pins to signal nets instead of providing their required capacitor connections to ground. This is a significant schematic-level fault that can prevent reliable operation of the flight-control and navigation processors."
}

